    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate is headlined by **Trevor Story**, who at a 75.93 score represents our strongest play. Facing R. Johnson, **Story** benefits from a high-efficiency park factor and an ideal wind direction, allowing his base projection to swell significantly against a vulnerable 5.22 xERA arm. Alongside him, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) is in a prime spot against Gallen; the combination of a favorable platoon edge and **Pasquantino**\u2019s recent form makes him an anchor for our counting stats. We are also leaning heavily into **Mickey Moniak** (68.75) and **James Wood** (65.96). **Wood**\u2019s elite .419 xwOBA at the leadoff spot provides a massive floor, and despite a slightly negative park factor, his high-volume plate appearance expectation makes him indispensable today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Cole Young**, whose 49.60 score fell just short of our target threshold. While he draws a favorable matchup against Bradford, his lower position in the batting order suppressed his ceiling compared to the primary lineup. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Seiya Suzuki** (46.29); his score is the lowest in the starting nine due to Henderson\u2019s difficult profile, but his spot at #2 in the order maintains his utility. We are also wary of **Griffin Conine**; while he is currently active, he faces an elite catcher with a 1.87s pop time, which effectively nullifies his utility in our scarcity-focused stolen base strategy.\n\nManagement remains concerned about the overall health of our speed-dependent depth. With **Corbin Carroll** absent from the lineup today, the burden of maintaining our SB category rests on the shoulders of **Jose Caballero** (58.59). Despite his #9 slot hitting against Sugano, we are forced to keep **Caballero** active solely for his speed upside. Our bench remains deep with reliable bats like **Austin Riley** and **Isaac Paredes**, but given the favorable xERA metrics facing our starting infielders, we are sticking with the current configuration to maximize our daily efficiency points.",
